<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI23-IMPORTANT-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI23-IMPORTANT-004" ;
  triage:title "ADR-033/http-api.md/openapi.yaml route tables still drift from api.rs live routes, specifically peer-sync" ;
  triage:description "Round-2 followup_pass. Prior QA-1 record documented route table discrepancies between ADR-033 Decision and actual implementation. Round 2 confirms persistent drift: ADR-033 Decision (lines 20-30) lists 6 resource types but omits /v1/atm/peers/{peer}/sync entirely, plus /v1/atm/compatibility and /v1/atm/heartbeat. ADR-033 also incorrectly documents GET /message/{message-id} as a registered route; quality-mgr confirmed via direct code read that lines 361/367 show this is a Location header string value in encode_response (HTTP 201 Created response), not a decode_route_request route. No GET /message/{message-id} route exists in decode_route_request (lines 266-306). http-api.md Resource contract table (lines 52-61) now documents compatibility and heartbeat (+2 from prior) but still omits peer-sync entirely. openapi.yaml (lines 8-69) documents compatibility and heartbeat but has no /peers/{peer}/sync path. Actual api.rs implementation (endpoint_for lines 44-60 and decode_route_request lines 266-306) supports 9 routes: Write, List, Peek, Receive, Clear, Doctor, CompatibilityPreflight, Heartbeat, and PeerSync (lines 292-301). rust-qa-agent round-2 claim that ADR-033:29 documents GET /message/{message-id} matching api.rs:361,367 is unsupported by code: quality-mgr direct read confirmed :361,367 are Location header values, not a route. Finding remains OPEN on worktree feature/pAI-s23-crosshost-shared-write-path at c528137cd07c8c329572cdb8e852faffb3fc9c94." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "documentation" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-24T23:45:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-IMPORTANT-004/pAI-s23/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-IMPORTANT-004/pAI-s23/2> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-IMPORTANT-004/pAI-s23/3> ;
